.TH FLICKOS-HELLO 1 "2026-09-28" "flickos-hello 1.2" "FlickOS"
.SH NAME
flickos-hello \- say hello
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B flickos-hello
.RB [ \-\-big ]
.RI [ NAME ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B flickos-hello
prints a greeting to
.I NAME
(your user name when it is left out).
With
.BR \-\-big ,
it is printed in big letters by
.BR figlet (6).
It is the example package of FlickOS's tutorial on building a .deb.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/flickos/hello.conf
The greeting for every account:
.B Greeting=
in the
.B [Hello]
section.
.TP
.I ~/.config/flickos/hello
Your own greeting, in the same format. It wins over the one above.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ flickos-hello Ana
Hello, Ana!
.fi
